  "confirmed_findings": [
    "8042 controller self-test (CMD 0xAA) consistently passes returning 0x55 in ~60ms",
    "8042 interface lines (CMD 0xAB) consistently pass returning 0x00 in ~322us (pull-up resistors intact)",
    "Port 0x60 input buffer is completely drained (0 bytes residue) before reset",
    "0xFF command consistently times out at internal hardware wire limit (~240ms) generating 0xFE",
    "0xAA clears Bit 6 timeout (0x7C -> 0x1C)",
    "0xAA sets default controller configuration to 0x30",
    "Writing 0x47 to controller configuration via 0x60 is verified accepted by readback (post-0xAE config is 0x47)",
    "Both PS/2 Interface 1 (0xAB) and Interface 2 (0xA9) consistently return 0x00 (LINES OK) indicating LPC Super I/O pull-up termination is electrically nominal",
    "Bypassing xHCI BIOS handoff does not restore Port 60/64 response (Native UEFI does not trap Port 60/64)",
    "State machine correctly blocks cascading 0xF4/0xEE/0xED commands upon reset failure",
    "Autonomous loop (Wake -> Boot -> Capture -> Ingest -> Shutdown -> 5s Settle -> Wake -> Re-verify) is 100% verified on real hardware"
  ],
  "disproven_hypotheses": [
    "Mouse byte collision causing 0xFE (AUX bit was proven 0 on all 0xFE responses)",
    "Stale buffer residue (Drained count was 0 bytes across all tests)",
    "LED subsystem bug (Failure occurs upstream on all commands 0xFF, 0xF4, 0xEE, 0xED)",
    "Controller Configuration bit 4 inhibiting clock (Verified accepted as 0x47 with clock enabled, yet 240ms timeout persisted identically)",
    "xHCI BIOS handoff killing SMM Port 60/64 emulation (Bypassing xHCI showed identical 240ms timeout in Native UEFI mode)"
  ],
  "active_hypotheses": [
    "Physical Device Connection: The keyboard is plugged into a USB port, not the physical PS/2 port, and Native UEFI firmware does not emulate Port 60/64 without CSM.",
    "Dual-Channel Routing: The motherboard PS/2 combo connector is wired to Channel 2 (AUX/Mouse), requiring Command 0xD4 prefix to route bytes to the keyboard.",
    "Port 0xAE hardware gate requires extended hardware line settling delay before accepting device transmission."
  ],
